WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.630 --> 00:00:01.900
It was announced today
that there was a change

00:00:01.900 --> 00:00:04.830
in leadership at Krispy Kreme Doughnuts.

00:00:04.830 --> 00:00:05.820
Uh yeah, it's a big company.

00:00:05.820 --> 00:00:08.760
Apparently Stephen Cooper
will no longer be the CEO,

00:00:08.760 --> 00:00:11.180
and former Kraft Foods divisional chief,

00:00:11.180 --> 00:00:13.925
Daryl Brewster is stepping
in to replace him.

00:00:13.925 --> 00:00:15.840
Wait, wait, wait, wait, wait, wait, Conan.

00:00:15.840 --> 00:00:18.250
Did you just say Daryl
Brewster is gonna be running

00:00:18.250 --> 00:00:22.230
Krispy Kreme Doughnuts
instead of Stephen Cooper?

00:00:22.230 --> 00:00:23.127
Yeah, yeah, that's right, yeah.

00:00:23.127 --> 00:00:24.700
No, no, man!

00:00:24.700 --> 00:00:26.345
That can't be happening!

00:00:26.345 --> 00:00:27.178
(audience laughing)

00:00:27.178 --> 00:00:30.680
Daryl Brewster's running
Krispy Kreme Doughnuts?!

00:00:30.680 --> 00:00:32.920
There's no reason to live!

00:00:32.920 --> 00:00:34.860
Where's my kayak?

00:00:34.860 --> 00:00:36.864
Where's my kayak?

00:00:36.864 --> 00:00:39.365
(grunting)

00:00:39.365 --> 00:00:43.448
Daryl Brewster is ruining
Krispy Kreme Doughnuts!

00:00:45.581 --> 00:00:49.664
(audience cheering and applause)

00:00:51.927 --> 00:00:54.874
Oh my god! That poor guy!

00:00:54.874 --> 00:00:55.998
[Brian] I'm okay! I'm okay!

00:00:55.998 --> 00:00:57.157
Oh!

00:00:57.157 --> 00:01:00.157
(audience cheering)

00:01:02.409 --> 00:01:04.677
I nailed the landing, Conan!

00:01:04.677 --> 00:01:07.110
I'm ready to see more of the show!

00:01:07.110 --> 00:01:08.470
All right well that's great,

00:01:08.470 --> 00:01:09.303
I'm glad you're okay.

00:01:09.303 --> 00:01:12.830
Unfortunately your seat
has already been filled.

00:01:12.830 --> 00:01:13.663
Yeah.

00:01:13.663 --> 00:01:14.760
(audience laughing)

00:01:14.760 --> 00:01:17.910
But if you want there's
still room in the back.

00:01:17.910 --> 00:01:19.440
Sit in the back?

00:01:19.440 --> 00:01:20.310
With those people?

00:01:20.310 --> 00:01:22.840
Those are the worst
seats in the house, man!

00:01:22.840 --> 00:01:25.760
If I have to sit back there,
there's no reason to live.

00:01:25.760 --> 00:01:28.035
No reason to live!

00:01:28.035 --> 00:01:29.302
Where's my bicycle?

00:01:29.302 --> 00:01:30.402
(audience cheering)

00:01:30.402 --> 00:01:31.985
Where's my bicycle?

00:01:34.573 --> 00:01:36.906
(screaming)

00:01:37.779 --> 00:01:38.779
Oh my god.

00:01:40.570 --> 00:01:43.360
I never knew there was
an iron suspension bridge

00:01:43.360 --> 00:01:45.146
outside our center.

00:01:45.146 --> 00:01:46.750
(audience laughing)

00:01:46.750 --> 00:01:49.360
And I've been here a long time.

00:01:49.360 --> 00:01:50.500
I should look around more.

00:01:50.500 --> 00:01:51.837
Well my apologies to the viewers-

00:01:51.837 --> 00:01:53.341
I nailed the landing!

00:01:53.341 --> 00:01:54.386
[Conan] Oh, hey!

00:01:54.386 --> 00:01:57.386
(audience cheering)

00:01:58.272 --> 00:02:00.272
Glad you're okay, wow.

00:02:02.509 --> 00:02:03.342
Order up!

00:02:03.342 --> 00:02:04.900
Okay now, you know what, I'm sorry sir,

00:02:04.900 --> 00:02:06.120
you're just gonna have to, I'm sorry,

00:02:06.120 --> 00:02:09.230
but you have to stop
pretending to kill yourself.

00:02:09.230 --> 00:02:10.570
It's a big waste of time,

00:02:10.570 --> 00:02:12.770
and it's distracting people from the show.

00:02:12.770 --> 00:02:15.381
I can't pretend to kill myself anymore?

00:02:15.381 --> 00:02:16.214
(audience laughing)

00:02:16.214 --> 00:02:17.500
I'm sorry, no, you can't.

00:02:17.500 --> 00:02:19.158
I can't pretend to kill myself?!

00:02:19.158 --> 00:02:20.334
There's no reason to live!

00:02:20.334 --> 00:02:21.684
[Conan] Oh, for God's sake.

00:02:21.684 --> 00:02:22.983
Where's my train?

00:02:22.983 --> 00:02:23.816
(audience cheering)

00:02:23.816 --> 00:02:25.233
Where's my train?

00:02:28.290 --> 00:02:30.090
Take me away, choo choo!

00:02:30.090 --> 00:02:32.813
(train horn)

00:02:32.813 --> 00:02:35.733
(audience laughing)

00:02:35.733 --> 00:02:36.566
(explosion)

00:02:36.566 --> 00:02:38.530
(audience cheering)

00:02:38.530 --> 00:02:40.281
Did you say 60.5?

00:02:40.281 --> 00:02:41.114
(audience laughing)

00:02:41.114 --> 00:02:42.200
'Cause I thought the Institute

00:02:42.200 --> 00:02:45.060
for Supply Management's
Index for non-manufacturing

00:02:45.060 --> 00:02:47.986
business activity was at 59.0.

00:02:47.986 --> 00:02:49.026
(laughs)

00:02:49.026 --> 00:02:49.859
No, no, no, it's interesting.

00:02:49.859 --> 00:02:53.010
Analysts predicted it would be 59.0,

00:02:53.010 --> 00:02:55.120
but it's actually at 60.5.

00:02:55.120 --> 00:02:56.210
Oh, no, no, no.

00:02:56.210 --> 00:02:57.043
This can't be!

00:02:58.000 --> 00:03:00.487
I thought it was 59.0!

00:03:00.487 --> 00:03:02.550
There's no reason to live!

00:03:02.550 --> 00:03:03.750
There's no reason!

00:03:03.750 --> 00:03:04.925
Where's my kayak?

00:03:04.925 --> 00:03:05.758
(audience cheering)

00:03:05.758 --> 00:03:06.591
Huh, why?

00:03:06.591 --> 00:03:07.922
(audience cheering)

00:03:07.922 --> 00:03:09.621
No, no reason!

00:03:09.621 --> 00:03:11.528
(audience applause and laughter)

00:03:11.528 --> 00:03:14.695
(prolonged screaming)

00:03:35.570 --> 00:03:37.620
Okay, now everyone settle,
I know that was upsetting,

00:03:37.620 --> 00:03:41.050
but just relax, 'cause
we've done this before,

00:03:41.050 --> 00:03:42.790
and usually by this time, that guy

00:03:42.790 --> 00:03:45.220
